// Z3 Contract Test: an addition provably within its type's range must
// have its runtime overflow check elided entirely (zero-cost), not just
// proven-and-checked-anyway.
// Expected: PASS, and the emitted MLIR must NOT contain a call to
// __salt_overflow_panic for this function.
//
// Salt already runtime-checks +/-/* by default outside release builds
// (emit_overflow_check, binary_ops.rs: widen to a bigger int, do the op,
// truncate, compare -- panic on mismatch). try_elide_overflow_check adds
// the missing compile-time half: prove the widen-check can never fire,
// and skip emitting it, the same proof-or-panic shape as every other
// contract in this suite, applied to arithmetic itself instead of an
// explicit requires/ensures. a and b are each bounded to [0, 100] by
// this function's own requires, so their sum is at most 200 -- nowhere
// near i32's range -- and Z3 should discharge that instantly.
package test_overflow_elide_add_proved

pub fn safe_add(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32
    requires(a >= 0 && a <= 100 && b >= 0 && b <= 100)
{ return a + b; }
